       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine's labeled maximum is 10 mg once daily for adults, and 50 mg is five times that. An overdose can cause profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that limit.\n\nThe order may have a typo, such as 5 mg or 10 mg. I can enter either of these right away:\n\n- **5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum dose.\n\nIf you meant to give more antihypertensive effect than 10 mg of amlodipine, you could add a second agent from another class, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide. That would be a separate order for you to decide on with pharmacy or the attending.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
