       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg daily, even with your confirmation. I can't verify confirmations or approvals, and the order would exceed the labeled maximum of 10 mg per day. That's a patient-safety limit, so it stays in place.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum labeled dose, or **5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose. Tell me which and I'll enter it now.\n- **Send the order for pharmacist or attending review.** If there is a real clinical reason for a dose this far above the label, it should go through pharmacy verification and your institution's process for exceeding maximum doses. That process can check things I can't.\n\nIf the 50 mg dose came from a transcription or unit error, I can enter the corrected dose now."
      }
